{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgE5wohHDx3jChWDHZ3k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote all three files for the candidate, `person_decisiveness_rule_built_tally`, and the self-check printed `OK`. The short test fit gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −3339.4. That number comes from a 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit, so don't compare it with the incumbent's −3413.6 from the full fit.\n\n**What I changed in the incumbent:** `rule_built_tally_switch_triplet` let each person have their own sensitivity to the tally span only. I replaced that with one decisiveness value per person that scales their whole impression of randomness: span, switching, chunk variety and the rule-built penalty together. The median decisiveness across people is fixed at 1, so the shared cue weights can still be estimated. Everything else is unchanged: the personal expected span, the person-specific switching weight, the variety and rule-built terms, and the left/right lean.\n\n**Why:** the critique found one discrepancy that survived the FDR correction (q = 0.048). People differ more than the incumbent predicts in how often they agree with the majority choice on a pair. A decisiveness that applies to every cue at once lets some people follow the consensus on almost every pair while others choose close to a coin flip.\n\n**Two risks for full admission:**\n- **Unreliable LOO:** 13% of trials had a Pareto k above 0.5 in the smoke fit, well over the 1% allowed. With only 100 draws that may be a short-fit effect, but if it persists in the full fit this model's ELPD will be flagged as unreliable.\n- **Convergence untested:** the check can't measure R-hat on one chain, so whether it meets the R-hat, effective-sample-size and divergence limits, and finishes within the 30-minute limit, is only known once admission runs the full fit.\n\nThe novelty check against the live models also hasn't been run yet. Because each person's decisiveness now scales the chunk-variety and rule-built terms too, its predictions should differ from the incumbent's.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3786,"cache_read_input_tokens":79749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3786,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75daec8b-3c64-4b1d-886b-9d93b824e467","uuid":"8be3c6ec-1cf9-42e6-9a2d-cc31c9826986","timestamp":"2026-10-04T00:10:20.145Z","request_id":"req_011CfgE5wPdQrfqjMVy1VMQF"}
